# SurfBud — Architecture Decisions

## Repo
One GitHub repo, three independent folders: `api/` `dashboard/` `extension/` — each deploys independently via path-filtered CI. No shared build-time code. Runtime communication only via HTTPS REST + WebSocket.

## Layer Rule — Non-Negotiable
```
Route → Controller → Service → Repository → Model

Controller   imports Services only
Service      imports Repositories + other Services
Repository   imports Models only
```
Never import a Model in a Controller. Never write DB queries in a Service. No exceptions.

## Three Critical Patterns
```
1. AI is always async       → BullMQ queue, never inline in request handler
2. Metrics are pre-computed → read UserMetrics document, never aggregate on demand
3. WebSocket sends deltas   → never full dataset, user-specific rooms only
```

## Auth
Access token 15min (Authorization header) + refresh token 7d (httpOnly cookie + Redis). No `plan` claim in JWT — no tiers in Phase 1.

## Phase 1
No Free/Pro tiers. No feature gating. Full product for all users. Monetization is Phase 3.

## Shared Types
`src/types/shared/` is duplicated across all three folders. Any change must update all three in one commit.
